sections.body:
The dictionary has three words for freshwater catfish [ref:hershberger1982]:

- **[julaji](word:julaji)**, the *[Yalanji](word:yalanji)* dialect word;
- **[kanyaji](word:kanyaji)**, the *Nyungkul* word, with *[julaji](word:julaji)* given as its Yalanji equivalent;
- **[walarrji](word:walarrji)**, literally 'with whiskers', which the dictionary says freshwater catfish 'are sometimes called'. It is built on **[walarr](word:walarr)** 'whiskers, beard'.

The sea and estuary catfish have their own names: **[kalu](word:kalu)** and **[kijukum](word:kijukum)**, both 'salt water catfish'. The dictionary also lists a separate *[kalu](word:kalu)* meaning 'garfish', so check which fish a speaker means [ref:hershberger1982].

These words come from Bloomfield and Daintree speakers. Western Yalanji people on the Mitchell and Palmer may use the same words or their own.
